9>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in a table, shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,-1)$ | $-1$ | $(-1,1)$ | $1$ | $(1,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $-2$ |  | $0$ |  | $2$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $+$ | $0$ | $-$ | $0$ | $+$ |\n| $f$ | $↗$ | max | $↘$ | min | $↗$ |\n\nFinally, let's use the table above to classify the critical points.\n\n- At $x=-1,$ the first derivative changes sign from positive to negative. Therefore, $x=-1$ is a local maximum.\n\n- At $x=1,$ the first derivative changes sign from negative to positive. Therefore, $x=1$ is a local minimum.\n\nWe conclude that $f(x)$ has one local minimum at $x=1.$" 13194139534682 true] [17592186303215 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303216 13194139534682 true] [17592186303215 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303217 13194139534682 true] [17592186303215 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303218 13194139534682 true] [17592186303215 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303219 13194139534682 true] [17592186303215 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303220 13194139534682 true] [17592186303215 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534682 true] [17592186303215 1041 "selection" 13194139534682 true] [17592186303215 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303218 13194139534682 true] [17592186303215 1110 #uuid "5f55c3cf-eb7e-55ec-9964-c22648d9cd49" 13194139534682 true] [17592186303216 1034 "3" 13194139534682 true] [17592186303216 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534682 true] [17592186303216 1111 #uuid "be612e63-2e38-5877-b165-01182404ce82" 13194139534682 true] [17592186303217 1034 "$f(x)$ does not have any local minima" 13194139534682 true] [17592186303217 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534682 true] [17592186303217 1111 #uuid "9ae10881-e54e-5906-9ce5-d2eac7acf29a" 13194139534682 true] [17592186303218 1034 "1" 13194139534682 true] [17592186303218 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534682 true] [17592186303218 1111 #uuid "9a518d61-c933-5b78-b9d9-8e84118fb384" 13194139534682 true] [17592186303219 1034 "-1" 13194139534682 true] [17592186303219 1103 #e